This product depends on software from the mcp-abap-adt and llm-agent projects
(https://github.com/fr0ster/mcp-abap-adt, https://github.com/fr0ster/llm-agent).
The list below is what this product actually ships, and it changes when the
dependencies do — regenerate it from the lockfile rather than editing by hand.

Apache-2.0

  @mcp-abap-adt/lib               the ADT handlers and the embeddable MCP server

LGPL-3.0-only

  @mcp-abap-adt/llm-agent         and llm-agent-libs, llm-agent-mcp, llm-agent-rag
  @mcp-abap-adt/anthropic-llm     and deepseek-llm, openai-llm, sap-aicore-llm
  @mcp-abap-adt/openai-embedder   and ollama-embedder, sap-aicore-embedder
  @mcp-abap-adt/qdrant-rag
  @mcp-abap-adt/sap-aicore-auth
  @mcp-abap-adt/adt-clients       and adt-strategies, connection, logger
  @mcp-abap-adt/auth-broker       and auth-providers, auth-stores
  @mcp-abap-adt/header-validator
  @mcp-abap-adt/interfaces-adt    and interfaces-adt-connection, interfaces-auth,
                                  interfaces-auth-sap, interfaces-network,
                                  interfaces-utils

GPL-3.0-only, development only

  @mcp-abap-adt/proxy             a local command-line proxy for development. It is
                                  a devDependency, runs as a separate process, and
                                  is not part of the built service (gen/srv).

The LGPL-3.0-only packages are linked at runtime, as ordinary npm dependencies
resolved from node_modules. Nothing is bundled: this product ships no browser
bundle containing them and performs no static linking. Their terms apply to
those packages, not to the code that links them. Any distribution of this
product must carry their licence text and leave the recipient able to replace
them with a modified version — which, given they remain separate packages on
disk, means replacing a directory.

Two sibling packages are deliberately NOT dependencies of this product:
@mcp-abap-adt/core, the standalone ADT MCP server (AGPL-3.0-only), and
@mcp-abap-adt/llm-agent-server (GPL-3.0-only). This product embeds the library
halves instead.

